### OPUS REVIEW 3 — DIF-READINESS UPGRADES (2026-03-24)

> Full analysis of 18 Opus recommendations against this 8,656-line plan.
> Classified as CRITICAL / HIGH / SPEC-NOTE. Adds 18 new checklist items.
> See Section 51 for the full analysis with rationale and implementation guidance.

**CRITICAL (blocks DIF credibility — do before DIF presentation):**
- ⬜ Simulation harness — Monte Carlo, 10K agents × 100K rounds, parameterized attacks (Sybil 5/10/50, bust-out, cartels 3/5/10). Publish results as spec appendix. Transforms Section 47 from "we believe" to "we measured." (Opus #1)
- ⬜ Deterministic arithmetic spec — fixed-point with 6 decimal places, integer weights (successRate=3500 meaning 35.00%), reference test vectors with exact intermediate values. Without this, two honest implementations produce different scores and fraud proofs collapse. (Opus #16)
- ⬜ Standalone threat model document — extract from Sections 20, 26, 32, 39, 41, 43, 44, 45 into single AID Threat Model doc in aid-spec repo. Adversary classes, attack trees, cost/impact/mitigation per vector. Standard practice for IETF/W3C. (Opus #15)

**HIGH (significant spec improvements — do in 10/10 plan or shortly after):**
- ⬜ AvoidFlagDeclaration in CDDL — flaggingValidator, reason enum (spam/fraud/copyright/malicious), evidence (receipt IDs), quorum (min 3 validators trust >60), appealWindow (72h), expiresAt. Level 2 conformance requirement. (Opus #4)
- ⬜ Receipt schema evolution policy — minor versions strictly additive (new optional fields only), major versions 6-month dual-support, verifiers MUST accept ≥ min supported version, unknown fields MUST be preserved (not stripped) when forwarding. Add to spec Section 19.13. (Opus #5)
- ⬜ EigenTrust seed rotation — every 500 new nodes, re-evaluate seeds from full graph (not bootstrap set). Seeds are not permanent. Prevents early-mover calcification. Add to 10/10 Day 3. (Opus #2)
- ⬜ Bloom filter commitment log summaries — each agent publishes Bloom filter of receipt hashes alongside Merkle root. Cross-reference is O(1) per pair (not O(n²)). Full cross-ref only on Bloom mismatch. 99%+ cost reduction. Add to 10/10 Day 1. (Opus #3)
- ⬜ Commitment log epoch compaction — after 30-day epoch, old entries Merkle-summarized into single root, individual entries prunable. Epoch summary chains to next. Bounds storage to O(epochs × summary_size). Add to 10/10 Day 1. (Opus #6)
- ⬜ Guardian precision tracking — guardianPrecision = correct_freezes / total_freezes. Precision <0.8 → demoted to alert-only. Precision <0.5 → removed from registry. Publish precision publicly. (Opus #9)
- ⬜ Per-service configurable timestamp window — maxTimestampSkew in ServiceListing CDDL + heartbeat. Protocol max 300s, recommended default 60s. High-frequency (DeFi) set 15s. (Opus #7)
- ⬜ Dual-hash receipts for PQC — add hashAlgorithm field to DSIR CDDL. Phase 2+ receipts SHOULD dual-hash SHA-256 + SHA-3-256. Verifiers accept either. When SHA-256 deprecated, SHA-3 proofs remain valid. One extra hash per receipt. (Opus #8)
- ⬜ E2E scenario conformance test suite — multi-step tests: register → 10 txs → feedback → score update → present passport → verify offline. Catches integration bugs test vectors miss. DIF expects conformance suites. (Opus #18)
- ⬜ Profile registry governance — profiles published in aidprotocol/aid-spec, each with unique ID, version, status (draft/active/deprecated). New profiles require 2 community reviews + 1 maintainer approval. W3C Note process adapted. (Opus #17)

