#### A.4 Trust Stack (5 Layers)

```
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|  LAYER 5: MARKET SIGNAL                                          |
|  Bonding curve pricing -- market prices reputation directly      |
|  Self-correcting, ungameable (costs real money to manipulate).   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|  LAYER 4: COMMUNITY SIGNAL                                       |
|  Weighted reviews + validator verdicts (anti-Sybil)              |
|  Reviews from high-spend wallets = 3x weight.                    |
|  Reviews from wallets with attestation history = 5x weight.      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|  LAYER 3: BEHAVIORAL SIGNAL                                      |
|  Attestation history + outcome reporting feedback loop           |
|  Every query generates a receiptId. Report success/failure.      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|  LAYER 2: CRYPTOGRAPHIC IDENTITY                                  |
|  Self-certifying DIDs, Ed25519 keypairs, Merkle proofs           |
|  DID = did:key:{publicKeyMultibase} -- public key IS the ID.    |
|  Offline-verifiable. No registry lookup needed. Portable.        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|  LAYER 1: PAYMENT                                                 |
|  Direct EIP-3009 settlement on Base L2 (no facilitator)          |
|  Extends x402 payment headers (backwards-compatible).            |
|  Trust-gated pricing: higher trust = lower price + deferred pay. |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
```

