#### A.7 Trust Verdicts

Trust verdicts and identity tiers are **two separate systems**:

- **Identity tiers** (anonymous/basic/verified/proven/trusted) = WHAT the agent has done to prove who they are. Determines verification multiplier (1.0x-1.2x).
- **Trust verdicts** (new/building/caution/standard/trusted/proceed) = HOW well the agent performs. Determined by the trust score formula.
- **`avoid` flag** is NOT a score-based tier. It is a manual flag applied by validators or triggered by structured reports (spam, fraud, copyright). An agent can have trust score 70 and still be flagged `avoid` if validators identify malicious behavior. Flagged agents are excluded from trust-gated pricing and revert to prepay-only.

An agent can be `verified` (identity tier) but `caution` (trust verdict) -- they proved their identity but have a mediocre track record. The verification multiplier boosts the raw trust score, but a low raw score with 1.1x multiplier is still low.

