#### A.9 Dual Crypto Layers: Ed25519 (Identity) + EIP-712 (Payment)

AID uses a dual-layer signing architecture. The two layers serve fundamentally different purposes:

**Layer 1: EIP-712 / ECDSA (Payment)**

| EIP-712 Limitation | Impact | AID Extension |
|--------------------|--------|----------------|
| No identity semantics | "This key signed this" -- not WHO signed it | AID DID embedded in every signed message |
| Single-signer model | No native dual-signing | Payer + provider both sign every receipt |
| No replay protection built-in | Apps must build their own nonces | Receipt IDs + Merkle anchoring = inherent replay protection |
| No conditional execution | All-or-nothing signatures | Trust-gated settlement: immediate/batched/deferred |
| EVM-only | Ethereum signing standard | Ed25519 (works everywhere: EVM, Solana, off-chain) |

```
Immediate: Agent signs EIP-3009 receiveWithAuthorization via ECDSA (secp256k1)
  -> Server calls receiveWithAuthorization (requires msg.sender == to, no front-running)
Batched/Deferred: Agent signs EIP-2612 permit (daily/weekly spending allowance)
  -> Server calls transferFrom for batch totals within allowance
Both methods handle USDC settlement on Base L2, x402-compatible
```

**Layer 2: Ed25519 (Identity + Trust)**
```
Agent signs request body with Ed25519 private key
  -> Proves DID ownership (self-certifying)
  -> Carries trust score, capabilities, Merkle proof
  -> Verifiable offline -- no RPC needed
  -> Works across chains (not bound to EVM)
```

**Combined in AID:**
```
PAYMENT-SIGNATURE: <EIP-712/EIP-3009 signed auth>     <- EVM payment
X-AID-PROOF:       <Ed25519 sig over request body>      <- Universal identity
```

This dual-layer approach means AID is BACKWARDS-COMPATIBLE with x402 (the PAYMENT-SIGNATURE header works with any x402 facilitator) while ADDING identity, trust, and offline verification through the Ed25519 layer.

**Dual-key architecture:** Every AID agent has two keys:
```
Ed25519 key pair    -> Identity (DID, signing requests, Merkle proofs)
secp256k1 key pair  -> Payment (EIP-3009, EVM transactions)

Linked via AID document:
{
  "publicKey": { "type": "Ed25519VerificationKey2020", "publicKeyMultibase": "zABC..." },
  "paymentAddress": { "chain": "base", "address": "0x742..." }
}
```

The Ed25519 key is generated at AID registration. The secp256k1 key (EVM wallet) is either provided by the agent (BYOK), generated by the server (returned once), or linked later via `PATCH /v1/aid/:did`.

**On-chain type definitions (future -- on-chain composability):**

```solidity
// Agent Identity struct for on-chain verification
struct AgentIdentity {
    bytes32 agentDid;           // keccak256 of DID string
    address principalAddress;   // human owner
    uint256 delegatedBudget;    // spending cap in USDC (6 decimals)
    bytes32 capabilityHash;     // hash of authorized action scopes
    uint256 expiresAt;          // unix timestamp
    bytes32 trustSnapshotHash;  // hash of latest trust snapshot
}

// Dual-signed service agreement
struct ServiceAgreement {
    bytes32 buyerDid;
    bytes32 sellerDid;
    bytes32 serviceHash;        // hash of service description
    uint256 price;              // USDC amount (6 decimals)
    uint256 maxLatencyMs;       // SLA constraint
    uint8   minTrustScore;      // minimum trust score required
    uint256 validUntil;
}

// Receipt for on-chain anchoring
struct X204Receipt {
    bytes32 receiptId;
    bytes32 payerDid;
    bytes32 providerDid;
    uint256 amount;
    bytes32 resultHash;         // SHA-256 of service result (truncated to bytes32 for EVM)
    bytes32 merkleRoot;         // trust chain snapshot
    uint256 timestamp;
}
```

