#### D.5 Error Semantics (HTTP Status Codes + Error Body)

Two implementations returning different status codes for the same error condition breaks interoperability. Error semantics are as important as success semantics.

```
AID ERROR CODE              HTTP STATUS   WHEN
------------------------    -----------   -------------------------------------
AID_PAYMENT_REQUIRED        402           No PAYMENT-SIGNATURE header, or
                                          insufficient funds for trust tier
AID_SIGNATURE_INVALID       401           X-AID-PROOF verification failed
AID_TIMESTAMP_EXPIRED       401           |now - timestamp| > allowed window
AID_DID_NOT_FOUND           404           DID not in registry (or tombstoned)
AID_TRUST_GATE_BLOCKED      403           Trust score below service minimum
AID_NONCE_REUSED            409           Nonce already seen in window
AID_VERSION_UNSUPPORTED     406           X-AID-VERSION not supported
AID_SETTLEMENT_FAILED       502           On-chain settlement reverted
AID_PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE    503           Provider DID's service is offline
AID_RATE_LIMITED             429           Too many requests for trust tier
```

```cddl
; Error Response Body (CDDL)

AidErrorResponse = {
  error:    text,                       ; human-readable message
  code:     aid-error-code,             ; machine-readable code
  ? details: text,                      ; additional context
  ? retryAfter: uint,                   ; seconds until retry (for 429)
  ? supportedVersions: [+ version-string],  ; for 406 responses
  ? trustGate: TrustGateInfo,           ; for 403 responses
}

TrustGateInfo = {
  required:   uint,                     ; minimum trust score for this service
  current:    float16,                  ; caller's current trust score
  verdict:    verdict,                  ; caller's current verdict
  upgradeUrl: ? text,                   ; URL with guidance on improving score
}

aid-error-code = "AID_PAYMENT_REQUIRED"
               / "AID_SIGNATURE_INVALID"
               / "AID_TIMESTAMP_EXPIRED"
               / "AID_DID_NOT_FOUND"
               / "AID_TRUST_GATE_BLOCKED"
               / "AID_NONCE_REUSED"
               / "AID_VERSION_UNSUPPORTED"
               / "AID_SETTLEMENT_FAILED"
               / "AID_PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE"
               / "AID_RATE_LIMITED"
```

