#### D.6 Conformance Levels

```
LEVEL 1 -- AID CORE CONFORMANT:
  MUST implement:
    - Identity headers (X-AID-DID, X-AID-PROOF, X-AID-TIMESTAMP, X-AID-NONCE)
    - Signature verification (canonical signing input)
    - Receipt format (DSIR structure, dual signatures)
    - Heartbeat endpoint (GET /aid/heartbeat)
    - Error semantics (10 error codes)
  CAN verify trust but does NOT compute it.
  Example: @aidprotocol/mcp-trust middleware (verifies caller identity + trust,
           delegates scoring to a trust oracle)

LEVEL 2 -- AID TRUST CONFORMANT:
  MUST implement Level 1, PLUS:
    - Trust scoring using canonical formula (v1.0: 4 dimensions, or v1.1: 5 dimensions)
    - Trust verdicts (new -> proceed mapping)
    - Commitment log (append-only, Merkle-anchored)
    - Feedback endpoint (POST /aid/feedback)
    - Trust-gated pricing tiers
  CAN serve as a trust oracle for Level 1 implementations.
  Example: independent trust oracle operator

LEVEL 3 -- AID FULL CONFORMANT:
  MUST implement Level 2, PLUS:
    - Settlement modes (immediate, batched, deferred)
    - Dual-party commitment logs with cross-reference
    - DSIR generation (both-party signing)
    - Provider countersignature (X-AID-PROVIDER-PROOF)
    - Mutual authentication
    - Key rotation protocol
    - GDPR erasure endpoint (DELETE /v1/aid/:did)
  Example: ClawNet (full platform implementation)
```

**Conformance testing:** Each level has a corresponding test vector suite.
- Level 1 tests: signature verify, header parse, heartbeat schema, error codes.
- Level 2 tests: scoring formula determinism, verdict mapping, commitment log structure.
- Level 3 tests: full receipt lifecycle, settlement mode transitions, key rotation.

