#### D.8 Protocol/Product Boundary

If a DIF reviewer would test it, it's an AID endpoint and it MUST be pure protocol. If a paying customer uses it, it's a ClawNet endpoint and it can use credits.

**AID PROTOCOL ENDPOINTS (pure protocol -- no API keys, no credits):**

```
PUBLIC READ (no auth required, free, rate-limited by IP):
  GET  /v1/aid/:did               -- resolve agent identity
  GET  /v1/aid/:did/trust         -- trust vector + composite score + verdict
  GET  /v1/aid/:did/trust-chain   -- Merkle proof chain for offline verification
  GET  /v1/aid/:did/receipts      -- DSIRs + Merkle proofs + commitment log
  GET  /v1/aid/scoring-params     -- public scoring config (versioned formula)
  GET  /v1/aid/eigentrust/status  -- convergence monitoring
  GET  /.well-known/aid.json      -- protocol discovery endpoint
  GET  /aid/heartbeat             -- service discovery + pricing tiers

PUBLIC WRITE (no auth required, free, rate-limited):
  POST /v1/aid/verify             -- verify a trust score against Merkle proof
  POST /aid/provision             -- X-AID-NEW zero-auth onboarding (3/IP/24h)

AID-AUTHENTICATED (X-AID-DID + X-AID-PROOF + X-AID-NONCE -- Ed25519, no API key):
  POST /aid/feedback              -- outcome reporting (weighted by reporter trust)
  GET  /aid/heartbeat/consumer    -- personalized pricing + alerts
  GET  /v1/aid/:did/commitment-log -- commitment log Merkle root + proof

AID-AUTHENTICATED + PAYMENT (X-AID-* headers + PAYMENT-SIGNATURE -- pure x402/USDC):
  POST /aid/skills/:id            -- skill execution via USDC payment
  POST /aid/orchestrate           -- orchestration via USDC payment
  POST /aid/query/:id             -- data query via USDC payment
```

**CLAWNET PRODUCT ENDPOINTS (credit auth -- unchanged):**

```
API-KEY AUTHENTICATED (X-API-Key: cn-... -- existing ClawNet middleware):
  POST /v1/orchestrate            -- orchestration via credits
  POST /v1/skills/:id/invoke      -- skill execution via credits
  GET  /v1/skills                 -- marketplace browsing
  POST /v1/economy/*              -- economy features (transfers, webhooks, etc.)
  POST /v1/batch                  -- batch queries via credits
  GET  /v1/stream/orchestrate     -- streaming via credits
  All existing /v1/* routes       -- unchanged
```

**The boundary:**
```
              AID PROTOCOL LAYER                    CLAWNET PRODUCT LAYER
              (DIF standard)                        (business monetization)
              ----------------                      ---------------------
Auth:         X-AID-DID + X-AID-PROOF               X-API-Key: cn-...
Payment:      PAYMENT-SIGNATURE (USDC)               Credit deduction
Middleware:   aidVerify() -- Ed25519 only             checkApiKey() -- API key
Error codes:  AID_* (Section D.5)                     SNAKE_CASE_CODE
Billing:      Direct USDC or free (reads)             deductCredit()
Who tests it: DIF reviewers                           Paying customers
```

**AID protocol auth middleware (`aidProtocolAuth`):**
1. Extracts `X-AID-DID`, `X-AID-PROOF`, `X-AID-TIMESTAMP`, `X-AID-NONCE` from headers
2. Verifies Ed25519 signature against canonical signing input
3. Checks nonce uniqueness (Redis, 5-min TTL)
4. Sets `c.set('aidIdentity', { did, trustScore, verified })` on the Hono context
