### D. Game-Theoretic Analysis (DIF Appendix — Cost-to-Manipulate)

#### D.1 Why This Section Exists

DIF reviewers will ask: "What stops a rational adversary from gaming your scoring formula?" Intuitive arguments ("Sybil self-dealing scores near zero") are not sufficient. This section provides back-of-envelope cost-to-manipulate estimates for each dimension at each trust tier, and justifies the specific parameter choices in the formula.

#### D.2 Threat Model

**Adversary:** Rational agent with budget B, wants to reach trust tier T in minimum time/cost.
**Goal:** Compute the optimal attack strategy against the 5-dimension v1.1 formula.
**Constraint:** Adversary can create Sybil agents, generate fake transactions, and submit self-feedback, but MUST pay real transaction costs and cannot forge Ed25519 signatures.

#### D.3 Per-Dimension Cost-to-Manipulate

```
DIMENSION 1: successRate (weight: 35%)
  Target: 0.95 (needed for score 80+)
  Attack: Self-transact with Sybil agents, report all successes
  Cost:   Each transaction costs minimum 0.001 USDC (endpoint floor)
          Need ~200 transactions for volume signal → $0.20
  Defense: counterpartyDiversity (Dimension 5) tanks to near-zero
           because all counterparties are the same Sybil cluster.
           Net effect: high successRate × near-zero diversity = LOW composite score
  Effective cost to game WITH diversity defense: create 20+ funded Sybil wallets
           × 10+ txs each = 200+ txs × $0.001 + 20 wallet funding costs (~$1 each)
           = $20.20 minimum just for the Sybil infrastructure

DIMENSION 2: chainCoverage (weight: 20%)
  Target: 0.90 (hash-chain integrity)
  Attack: Cannot be faked — chain coverage measures the integrity of the agent's
          OWN attestation hash chain. Missing links = lower coverage.
          An attacker who selectively omits negative attestations breaks the chain.
  Cost:   $0 to maintain (just don't tamper with your chain)
          BUT: dual-party commitment logs (Section 10/10 Day 1) mean selective
          omission is detectable. Cost to maintain high coverage WHILE omitting
