### A. Strategic Positioning

#### The Paradigm Shift

The original AID positioning was: "one protocol to replace x402 + ERC-8004 + ERC-8183." **That positioning is wrong.** The market has moved past 3 protocols to 8+, and every single layer is missing the same thing: TRUST.

```
A2A (Google/AAIF)     -> Agent-to-agent communication    -> NO TRUST
MCP (Anthropic/AAIF)  -> Tool access (20,000+ servers)   -> NO TRUST
MCP-I (DIF/Vouched)   -> Identity + delegation for MCP   -> NO REPUTATION
ACP (Stripe + OpenAI) -> Consumer checkout for agents    -> NO AGENT SCORING
UCP (Google + Shopify) -> Product data for agents        -> NO TRUST
x402 (Coinbase)       -> Crypto micropayments            -> NO IDENTITY
ERC-8004              -> On-chain agent identity          -> NO CANONICAL SCORING
Agent Wallets          -> Key management                  -> NO REPUTATION
```

MCP won because it was ONE thing (tool access) that worked everywhere. A2A won because it was ONE thing (communication) that composed with MCP. Stripe won because it was ONE thing (payments) that worked everywhere. **AID wins by being ONE thing: TRUST -- that plugs into every protocol.**

#### The Reframing

```
OLD POSITIONING (monolith -- won't get mass adoption):
  "Use AID instead of x402 + ERC-8004 + ERC-8183"

NEW POSITIONING (layer -- plugs into everything):
  "Add AID trust to ANY protocol stack"

  MCP server       -> npm install @aidprotocol/mcp-trust     -> caller trust verification
  A2A agent card   -> AID trust score in metadata             -> trust-based routing
  ACP checkout     -> trust-gated pricing                     -> better agents pay less
  x402 payment     -> AID identity headers                    -> know who's paying
  UCP merchant     -> trust badges                            -> verified agent access
  ERC-8004         -> AID fills Validation Registry           -> canonical scoring
  AgentKit wallet  -> AID linked to wallet                    -> portable reputation
  CrewAI/LangGraph -> pip install aid-trust                   -> trust-scored agent hiring
```

**The one-sentence positioning:**
> "AID doesn't replace your payment rail, your identity registry, or your security scanner. It makes all of them smarter by adding scored, verifiable, portable trust."

#### The MCP Opportunity (20,000 Servers, Zero Trust)

MCP has 12,000-20,000 live servers with ZERO trust layer. MCP-I adds identity and delegation but NOT reputation. This is the single biggest opportunity.

**@aidprotocol/mcp-trust -- one-line trust integration for any MCP server:**

